--- serialize -- generic serialization to/from strings for the handl runtime.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `serialize` stdlib interface: 2 functions
--- covering serialization of `serde_json::Value` to a string (json/yaml/toml)
--- and deserialization of a string back into a `Value`. The Rust bridge in
--- `plugin-lib-utils` loads this file via `include_str!`, parses the `cap`
--- declarations for the plugin capability surface, and registers the Rust
--- handls (handlers) in an `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its
--- native Rust impl backed by a `SerializerRegistry`.
---
--- Both functions are FFI atoms (they delegate to `SerializerRegistry` from
--- `plugin-lib-serialize`, which wraps Json/Yaml/Toml serializers, and cannot
--- be expressed as pure handl arrows without losing the exact error messages
--- the tests rely on). The `op`/`handl` declaration form (ADR-0077 Phase 2)
--- declares the interface; the Rust `Function` impls in `ops.rs` provide the
--- logic.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- serialize.serialize -- serialize a value into a string using a named format.
--- serialize.deserialize -- deserialize a string into a value using a named format.
cap "serialize.serialize"
cap "serialize.deserialize"
op "serialize.serialize" : (Value * Value) -> String
  guarantee: True
op "serialize.deserialize" : (String * Value) -> Value
  guarantee: True
handl "serialize.serialize" = rust_serialize_serialize
handl "serialize.deserialize" = rust_serialize_deserialize
